          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A club is a particular sort of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrine"} doctrine
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} free
            algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(C)
            with respect to the monad, it frequently suffices to describe the free algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(1)
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+wreath+product"} categorical wreath product
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≀
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(C) \cong F(1) \wr C
          %p
            Examples of this phenomenon include the monad for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+categories"} symmetric monoidal categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+categories"} braided monoidal categories
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+category"} closed symmetric monoidal categories
          %p
            Clubs were introduced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"} Max Kelly
            in a series of papers (see references), and are akin in spirit to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operads
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategories"} generalized operads
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+monads"} polynomial monads
          %h2#clubs_over_the_permutation_category Clubs over the permutation category
          %p
            This is the most basic sort of club, introduced by Kelly in
            %a{:href => "#KellyMVFC"} MVFC
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#KellyAAC"} AAC
          %h3#action_by_substitution_product Action by substitution product
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}
            be the category of finite sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n] = \{1, \ldots, n\}
            (including the empty set
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            be the category of small categories. We define a “wreath product” action of the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat/\mathbf{P}
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat/\mathbf{P}
            is the slice category of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo :
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ: Cat/\mathbf{P} \times Cat \to Cat
          %p
            taking a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma: C \to \mathbf{P}, D)
            to the category whose objects are tuples
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c; d_1, \ldots, d_n)
          %p
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in Ob(C)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_i \in Ob(D)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(c) = [n]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f; g_1, \ldots, g_n)
          %p
            consisting of a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi c
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: c \to c'
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_i: d_i \to d_{\Gamma(f)(i)}'
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
            This generalizes the standard notion of wreath product: given a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and a permutation representation, i.e., a homomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma: G \to Aut([n]) \hookrightarrow \mathbf{P}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⋉
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \int H = G \ltimes H^n
          %p
            with the action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n
            induced from the action on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
          %p
            Another, more abstract, way to describe this substitution product is as follows: there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monad"} cartesian monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            whose algebras are symmetric strict monoidal categories, and we have
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mo =
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P} = S 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \circ D
            can then be described as the following pullback in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi D
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                          %mi D
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %mi S
                              %mo !
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi Γ
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{\Gamma \circ D &amp; \overset{}{\to} &amp; S D\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{S !}\\
                  C &amp; \underset{\Gamma}{\to} &amp; S 1 &amp; = \mathbf{P}}
          %p See below for a general version of this construction.
          %h3#substitution_product_as_monoidal_product Substitution product as monoidal product
          %p
            We describe how the substitution action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ
            lifts to a self-action denoted by the same symbol:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo :
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ: Cat/\mathbf{P} \times Cat/\mathbf{P} \to Cat/\mathbf{P}
          %p
            To start, given a pair
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma: C \to \mathbf{P}, \Delta: D \to \mathbf{P})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \circ \Delta
            is the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \circ D
            described above. The functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \circ \Delta: \Gamma \circ D \to \mathbf{P}
          %p
            sends an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c; d_1, \ldots, d_n)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_i \Delta(d_i)
          %p
            The effect of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \circ \Delta
            on morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f; g_1, \ldots, g_n)
            may be summarized as “substituting the permutations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(g_i)
            into the permutation
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(f)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}([n], [n]) = Aut(n)
            of permutations on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            may be identified with the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Lin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lin(n)
            of total (or linear) orders on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1, 2, \ldots, n\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Lin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(n) = Lin(n)
            are components of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Lin
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lin
            where the operadic multiplication
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Lin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Lin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi …
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Lin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Lin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(n; k_1, \ldots, k_n): Lin(n) \times Lin(k_1) \times \ldots \times Lin(k_n) \to Lin(k_1 + \ldots + k_n)
          %p
            takes a linear ordering of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            linearly ordered sets and produces the evident linear ordering on the disjoint sum of the sets.
          %p
            Then, given a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f; g_1, \ldots, g_n)
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \circ D
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo =
                    %mi def
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma \circ \Delta)(f; g_1, \ldots, g_n) \stackrel{def}{=} \mu(n; k_1, \ldots, k_n)(\Gamma(f), \Delta(g_1), \ldots \Delta(g_n))
          %p
            Given the abstract description above of the substitution product in terms of the cartesian monad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \circ \Delta
            can be described as the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi D
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi Δ
                  %mi T
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mn 1
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \circ D \to T D \overset{T \Delta}{\to} T T 1 \overset{\mu_1}{\to} T 1  = \mathbf{P}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu\colon T T \to T
            is the multiplication of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
