                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %strong algebra
            over the club is an algebra for this monad. Unlike in the covariant cases, this monad is
            %em not
            a 2-monad, but it does give a 2-monad if one restricts to the locally groupoidal 2-category of categories, functors, and natural isomorphisms.
          %h3#examples_2 Examples
          %p
            As shown above, we cannot expect to describe compact closed categories with a club. However, we can describe various other structures of mixed variance, such as symmetric monoidal
            %em closed
            categories. Specifically, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
