                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma: F(1) \to \mathbf{G}
            which takes a morphism of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(1)
            to its extranaturality graph. The crucial observation is that no basepoint morphism lies in the image of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cut-elimination+theorem"} cut-elimination theorem
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#KellyCET"} KellyCET
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multivariable+adjunction"} multi-variable right adjoints
            to any of the operations of a club over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}
